        <item>
            <key> <string>description</string> </key>
            <value> <string encoding="cdata"><![CDATA[

Run raw SQL on the instance database.\n
\n
connection_id defaults to \'erp5_sql_connection\'. Read-only statements\n
(SELECT/SHOW/DESCRIBE/EXPLAIN...) run freely; writes require allow_write=true.\n
\n
LIMIT: when the query has no LIMIT of its own, an automatic " LIMIT <max_rows+1>"\n
(default 51) is appended — a query that already ends in its own LIMIT (plain,\n
OFFSET or "offset, count" form) is passed through untouched, which used to\n
die with a confusing "1064 ... near \'LIMIT 51\'" (session issue B8). Rows are\n
capped at max_rows in Python when your own LIMIT governs.\n
\n
JSON safety: DateTime / datetime / date / time cells are serialized as ISO\n
strings, Decimal as text, bytes decoded (all truncated like text cells), so\n
a datetime column no longer kills the payload with "not JSON serializable".\n
\n
formats: \'rows\' (default), \'count\' (count + first row), \'summary\' (3 sample\n
rows), \'csv\'. max_rows is capped at 500.\n


]]></string> </value>
